# 5. Exclusions

The project will not attempt to become a comprehensive treatment of every environmental or natural-resource issue.

The following subjects are outside the project's primary scope unless they directly affect conservation outcomes:

* general energy policy;
* general economic policy;
* general climate policy;
* industrial policy;
* transportation policy;
* public-health policy;
* environmental justice as a standalone policy field;
* agricultural policy unrelated to conservation;
* international environmental policy unrelated to U.S. natural-resource management;
* unrelated environmental regulation;
* partisan campaign strategy; and
* electoral strategy.

These subjects may be discussed where they materially affect conservation outcomes, but they will not become independent policy pillars.

